;">The agenda</h2></div></td></tr>
<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Global stocks are in decline, as a near-9%=
 plunge in Nvidia shares in extended trading sent waves across Asian market=
s, on news that its board may oust longtime CEO Jensen Huang.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Nvidia shares fell as much as 8.8% in pre-=
market trading in New York, wiping another $360bn off the company=E2=80=99s=
 value. That takes losses this week to $640bn, a 14% decline.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Asian stock markets are a sea of red. Japa=
n=E2=80=99s Nikkei is down 0.7%, Hong Kong=E2=80=99s Hang Seng lost 1.3% an=
d South Korea=E2=80=99s Kospi fell nearly 0.6%, while Taiwan=E2=80=99s benc=
hmark index tumbled 2.6%.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">In China, the Shenzhen Composite slid 1.6%=
 and the CSI 300 dropped 0.87%.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Charu Chanana, the chief investment strate=
gist at Saxo Bank in Singapore, said: =E2=80=9CNvidia sits at the centre of=
 an increasingly interconnected AI ecosystem. Its turmoil comes when financ=
ing, hyperscaler capex, valuations and =E2=81=A0returns on AI investment we=
re already under scrutiny.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Nvidia=E2=80=99s board reportedly met late=
 Wednesday to decide whether to oust Huang, after he admitted to an affair =
with alleged Chinese spy Alice Huang. Beijing has rejected the spying alleg=
ations.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.thegua=
rdian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRzt4s6ftkaHQJFlmbtE71UEi4Swp1AsnMK1=
7mBwkPgckPzSqjLFjuO6Fjxt3MiPscXWNi3RywVLswmRV6L-1qbbHtP2H_GpCFIv94NednSIgs8=
VPzl5iR6zEap_M8qZSO4-pqrZl5zsdUcaPtv4VBjlncNbTbR81gORNMNksUlxQgZjLnJRqGQpYg=
PxhleQikeddhvbjcuVgZeCKqbzy8CZbUwzxUOT1PBB9iQABCv28Tha_bZrgM5sJV7pBCXEunw/4=
vo/jX2buUdbSX-WQUbGI6vsUw/h39/h001.OuxEJenPpCDNABhi4T-Pp2EsM8ovHS4Rg7Z_cvAF=
YUQ" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">The New York Times has reported</a> that Hua=
ng also had an affair with a company executive who reported to =E2=80=8Chim=
.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Jake Dollarhide, the chief executive of Lo=
ngbow Asset Management in Tulsa, Oklahoma, told Reuters: =E2=80=9CIt looks =
bad from every single angle. I believe the board won=E2=80=99t oust him unt=
il they have an all-star, a known entity in the tech sector, to replace him=
.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CAt the end of the day, let=E2=80=
=99s not forget that the Nvidia chip is the centrepiece of the AI story.=E2=
=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">It=E2=80=99s not yet clear who might repla=
ce Huang as CEO. In the meantime, Chinese domestic GPU makers surged on Thu=
